@@ -0,0 +1,90 @@
+# P12 full-diff review evidence
+
+Reviewed paper range: `399d22c..3ea8cc02f9c8cf79bf6477f08f36325f72cdfd1b`.
+Code snapshot: WSmart-Route `961acd78ca7b09c9231bb8b160589a6c9a1cd467`.
+The review covers all 13 changed paths, the resulting full manuscript,
+notation, cross-references, changed bibliography entries, generated tables,
+figures and owner rulings. Fixes are proposed in a separate patch, not changes
+to the archived experimental measurements. No simulator was run.
+
+## Mathematical checks
+
+Run `python Evidence/check_formulation.py` and `python Evidence/check_example.py`.
+These need only the Python standard library.
+
+The original residual-flow depot equations imply zero collection. Write
+`L=sum(q_i)`. Coupling and degree at the start/copy depots imply
+`sum(h_0j)=Qk` and `sum(h_j,end)=Qk-L`. The reversed equations also require
+`sum(h_end,j)=Qk-L` and `sum(h_j0)=Qk`. Summing residual conservation over
+bins then gives `L=Qk+(Qk-L)-Qk-(Qk-L)=0`. Correct residual flows travel on
+used directed arcs: `h_0j` leaves the real depot and `h_j,end` enters its copy.
+Forbidden depot arcs must additionally be fixed to zero.
+
+A zero-demand cycle satisfies both commodity balances and in/out degrees.
+It is excluded in the corrected reference formulation by internal-arc cuts.
+The implemented SWC-TCF solver has no such cuts; the paper now states that
+limitation rather than claiming its degree constraints exclude the cycle.
+
+The former initial-state assumption allowed `w=110`, `psi*E=100`, `a=10`,
+`U=110`; the first post-arrival amount is 120 and violates the purported
+bound. The revised bound includes `w+a^1` explicitly. Subsequent opening
+states are at most `psi*E`, by the force rule and complete collection.
+
+The force rule permits non-service at exact threshold equality. The patch
+states this explicitly; it does not introduce an epsilon gap. Overflow still
+counts equality exactly, as an inclusive post-solution reporting identity.
+The implemented SWC-TCF backstop, unlike the reference linear force rule,
+also forces equality. This remaining modelling distinction is visible for
+owner/Hector review.
+
+The independent example enumeration considers every ordered feasible route
+and disjoint pair, comparing travel plus vehicle costs with integer
+arithmetic. It finds 2,688 feasible visit-set trajectories (route reversal
+ties collapsed). Myopic profit is 45.28; rho=0 optimum is 60.532, collecting
+910 kg over 25.9 km and leaving 115 kg. That same trajectory valued at rho=R
+scores 71.48. The true rho=R optimum is 79.18: serve {1,3} on day 1 and nobody
+on days 2 and 3, collect 480 kg over 18.3 km, leave 545 kg. The old enumerator
+summed dictionary keys, `sum(w4)`, rather than terminal values, adding the
+constant 0.952 to every trajectory. This explains the erroneous old table.
+The complete symmetric matrix is explicitly an illustrative modification:
+slide 28 prints d04=10.0, not 9.8; d14 and d24 were not printed. The patch
+retains the existing matrix and labels those choices, without pretending
+that all eight slide distances were reproduced.
+
+## Evidence and publication checks
+
+- The read-only P10 archive audit was rerun unchanged. All 480 30-day rows
+  match raw logs on ten metrics; six table numerical bodies are unchanged.
+  The 224 improver pairs and 165 horizon pairs remain intact. See the P10
+  ledger for source files, hashes and deferred historical provenance.
+- SANS counter increments per neighbor evaluation, checks `>500` at block
+  end: `logic/src/policies/route_construction/meta_heuristics/` plus
+  `simulated_annealing_neighborhood_search/heuristics/sans.py:340-367`.
+- SWC flow directions and inclusive forcing are directly visible in
+  `logic/src/policies/route_construction/exact_and_decomposition_solvers/`
+  `smart_waste_collection_two_commodity_flow/gurobi.py:93-148`.
+- ALNS segment size 100 is a reviewed implementation default (`params.py:61`),
+  not an explicitly recorded archived setting. HGS counts are configured
+  `nb_elite` and `nb_close`, not necessarily extant sets of those sizes.
+- Ramos source PDF in `bibliography/policies/Smart_Waste_Collection-Two-Commodity_Flow.pdf`,
+  printed pages 150-151, uses 0.5 in the undirected objective (11). The
+  factor is restored only in the source recap; directed benchmark equations
+  retain full directed costs. Source case-study numbers are on pages 152-153.
+- Mes (2012) chapter metadata verified against the publisher:
+  [Springer chapter](https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-28777-0_13).
+  Correct book: *Use Cases of Discrete Event Simulation*, Springer,
+  pp. 277-307, editor Steffen Bangsow; not the InTech volume in the prior diff.
+- Baldacci (2004) title, authors, year and pages confirmed against
+  [INFORMS](https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/abs/10.1287/opre.1040.0111).
+- The malformed `@article{Mes2014InventoryRouting},` syntax is repaired so
+  BibTeX actually reads the entry fields, not merely its citation key.
+
+## Interpretation limits
+
+No historical source revision or missing demand dataset has been reconstructed.
+No capacity-feasibility, causal-stage-effect, stochastic-replication or historical
+optimality certificate follows from matching summary tables. Presentation-sourced
+raw appendix graphics retain their stated exclusion/provenance caveats. Existing
+literature citations are retained; this review does not claim a replication of
+all cited external studies. Owner Q8 recovery and subsequent rerun decisions
+remain open; venue/page budget remains unknown. Owner review precedes Hector's.
